                <pb facs="0480" n="362" sameAs="frus:frus1928v02/pg362"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">125.643/56: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in China</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">MacMurray</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-10-26T16:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">October 26,
                                1928—4 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>359. Your 748, October 5, 5 p.m. I have been willing to accede to your
                    recommendation not to force the issue: Nevertheless you are referred to the
                    series of previous instructions and I wish to know whether return of consular
                    officers to Nanking may be expected soon. I consider the presence of an American
                    official at the seat of government very desirable.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
